      "rev_n_5_85c5f5_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_85c5f5_1",
        "node_id": "n_5_85c5f5",
        "thought_text": "The error in the reasoning step is that it only checks if the average is an integer, which is not sufficient. We need to check if the absolute differences between A and K, and B and K, are equal. This requires a more comprehensive approach that considers both the parity (oddness or evenness) of the differences and their magnitudes.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "2169069464722954740",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_5_85c5f5_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_15af657494",
        "created_at": 1794516909.7801347
      },
      "rev_n_7_71da3f_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_71da3f_1",
        "node_id": "n_7_71da3f",
        "thought_text": "The error in the reasoning step is that calculating the average of A and B doesn't necessarily yield the correct solution. Instead, we should consider the properties of the absolute difference equation. The correct approach is to find a point where the absolute differences from both A and B are equal, which occurs when K is the midpoint between A and B.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "3044033089738070943",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_7_71da3f_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_d2ceda5e35",
        "created_at": 1794516924.3221986
      },
      "rev_n_6_f3eb47_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_f3eb47_1",
        "node_id": "n_6_f3eb47",
        "thought_text": "The error in the reasoning step is that the condition (a - k) == (b - k) is insufficient to determine if K exists. We need to check both (a - k) == (b - k) and (b - k) == (a - k) to ensure that K satisfies the condition |A - K| = |B - K|.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "2169069464722954740",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_6_f3eb47_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_a0e020cc05",
        "created_at": 1794516942.864131
      },
      "rev_n_12_b318df_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_12_b318df_1",
        "node_id": "n_12_b318df",
        "thought_text": "Refine the reasoning step: Instead of checking if k is equal to either a or b, we should verify if k satisfies the condition |A - K| = |B - K| by calculating both sides of the equation and comparing them. This approach will correctly identify when no solution exists and when a valid k is found.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "7169123885525953221",
